  "order": 0,
  "about": "One layout's key inventory for Hexboard. This file states which characters this layout offers, which panel they live on, and where on that panel they sit. Hexboard is a platform for layout variants: each variant is a config file of its own alongside this one, carrying its own id and name, and this file is the default layout the app ships with and falls back to when no other has been chosen — which is what isDefault marks. language is the BCP 47 tag of the language this layout is for, and is what the layout picker groups by; no display name is stored with it, because a reader's own device names a language from the tag in that reader's own language. order is this layout's position within its language, lower first, and a layout without one sorts after every layout that has one. Its scope is the three letter and symbol panels: the emoji panels reached by vertical swipe down are system-supplied content rather than a hand-curated inventory, so they are deliberately outside this file and the manifest rules below do not apply to them. resources/key-manifest.md is generated from this file by scripts/generate-key-manifest.py and must not be hand-edited. Geometry (zag offsets, circle radius, touch-target sizing, uppercase scaling, nearest-centre hit-testing) is deliberately NOT in this file: it lives in Kotlin, because it is the perceptual wedge SPEC calls inviolable. A variant may change which characters you get, never how it feels to aim at them.",
  "generates": "resources/key-manifest.md",
  "manifestRules": [
    "NO KEY MAY BE LOST. Every output character must appear in this manifest. Before shipping any build, run audit_keys.js and confirm the output set matches exactly.",
    "NO UNRESOLVED DUPLICATES. Each output character should appear on exactly one panel. Cross-panel duplicates must be resolved before shipping — either remove one instance and fill the vacated slot with something new, or explicitly justify why both are needed (e.g. a convenience copy that is clearly labelled).",
    "NO SILENT CHANGES. Any key move, addition, or removal must be reflected in this manifest and noted in the commit comment.",
    "EMPTY SLOTS ARE OPPORTUNITIES, NOT ACCEPTABLE GAPS. If a duplicate is removed, the freed slot must be filled with a character that has no other home, agreed with the user first."
  ],
  "rule1Note": "Rule 1 names `audit_keys.js`, which is a browser-prototype script. The wording is kept as written because it describes the prototype. The underlying principle — verify the shipped key set against this manifest before shipping — is what carries over to Android, where the mechanism will be different.",
  "nonConsumers": [
    "hexboard17.html — the browser prototype. Frozen: reference only, does not read this config.",
    "planning/layout-preview.html — the standing layout preview fixture. Does not read this config either; it stays hand-edited per CLAUDE.md."
  ],
